<http://data.silknow.org/object/5c15731c-beb5-361a-8bcb-2b3aa95e1be9>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Woman’s fancy dress stomacher made of pink silk satin, couched with silk cord and partially wrapped silver filé, parchment ‘leaves’ wrapped in pink silk floss and silk-wrapped purl, and embroidered with white and yellow silk floss. These are worked in French knots and satin stitch in a pattern of scrolling vines and flowers.  The embroidery was recycled and pieced to make a stomacher for 19th-century fancy dress, lined with white silk taffeta and edged with machine lace."@en , "F, fancy dress, 1850-70, British, made of pink silk embriodered with gimp, 1660-80, French"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/a2147526-8dd6-3bae-92df-6d6a70b44530> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f7754fc4-2515-38a1-8ed5-cdbc835f666a> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "F, fancy dress, 1850-70, British, made of pink silk embriodered with gimp, 1660-80, French"@en , "Woman’s fancy dress stomacher made of pink silk satin, couched with silk cord and partially wrapped silver filé, parchment ‘leaves’ wrapped in pink silk floss and silk-wrapped purl, and embroidered with white and yellow silk floss. These are worked in French knots and satin stitch in a pattern of scrolling vines and flowers.  The embroidery was recycled and pieced to make a stomacher for 19th-century fancy dress, lined with white silk taffeta and edged with machine lace."@en ;
